00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.820
CASSIE KOZYRKOV: With almost
500 sessions at Next 2019,

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:06.070
it's understandable that you
couldn't get to them all.

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:10.600
So if you didn't see AI Hub,
The One Place for Everything AI,

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:13.020
then stay tuned, because
here's the rewind.

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:16.492
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:20.380
The AI universe is
expanding, which

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:23.510
means you can get more creative
with it than ever before,

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:26.230
and the possibilities
are endless.

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:29.050
Unfortunately, it might
feel like the things

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:32.259
you need to learn to get
going are endless too.

00:00:32.259 --> 00:00:35.600
The space has grown huge,
messy, and daunting.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.700
So what if you could step
into a tight, parallel AI

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:41.680
universe that
combines everything

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:46.030
you need to make your experience
with building AI magical?

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:48.340
Welcome to AI Hub.

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.530
The vision behind
Google Cloud's AI Hub

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:53.290
is to give you a
10x force multiplier

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:55.480
by taking the
confusion, repetition,

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:58.730
and wheel reinvention
right out of your work.

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:01.390
AI Hub brings together a
number of managed services

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:03.120
to make your lives easier.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.980
And because AI is a
team sport, AI Hub

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:08.350
is designed with skills
diversity in mind

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:11.680
and focuses on making it
easy to do what you do best

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:13.870
and then share your
work with colleagues

00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:15.650
who love the other parts.

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:18.370
It's for the data scientist who
wants to work on the cutting

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:21.970
edge without the painful
slow going every time you

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:23.570
want to try something new.

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:25.090
It's for the app
developer looking

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:27.310
for that familiar
pattern of discovery

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:30.490
without getting dunked in the
mathematical nitty gritty.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:33.070
And it's for the machine
learning production engineer

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:35.500
who keeps getting asked
why the model took

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:39.850
three weeks to build but 10
months to put into production.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:43.060
Hint-- production
used to be hard.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:46.850
It's for the person who loves
point and click in a great UI

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:49.600
and for the person who likes
direct command line access.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:54.300
Whoever you are, if you
build with AI, it's for you.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:57.290
AI Hub isn't just a ski lift for
your machine learning chores.

00:01:57.290 --> 00:01:58.960
It's the whole resort.

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:01.990
And as a result, the talk is
quite frankly unsummarizable.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:04.543
It is just too dense
with incredible demos,

00:02:04.543 --> 00:02:06.460
and you'll definitely
want to experience them.

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:08.410
But here is a small taste.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:10.900
AI Hub features instant
VM and Jupyter Notebook

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:18.700
setup, a brain-friendly,
brilliantly

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:20.530
searchable repository
of code to get

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:25.270
you started, collaboration
tools, extra transfer learning

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:33.140
support, and Kubeflow
Fairing to jumpstart

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:35.900
your move to production
with ready-to-go, end-to-end

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:38.570
pipeline templates and
broken-down components

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:40.700
to help you mix
and match instead

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:42.380
of reinventing that wheel.

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:44.440
Oh, and don't forget
access to TFX.

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:47.210
That's TensorFlow
Extended, Google's recently

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:50.150
open-sourced, tailor-made
production machine learning

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:53.000
pipeline with advanced
model analytics capabilities

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.100
that accelerate your
development process,

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.770
helping you iterate
in a smarter direction

00:02:57.770 --> 00:03:00.270
to launch your
awesome system faster.

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:02.750
This is the power
to build quickly.

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:04.700
It's the joy of
collaborating without having

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:06.980
to take everything on
your own shoulders,

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:09.560
and it's the beauty of
enjoying a magical user

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:11.462
experience as an AI builder.

